# External software required by this Emacs config

Date: 2026-07-28
Derived from: `init.el`, `src/functions.el` (Emacs 30.2, Arch Linux)

Scope: **non-Emacs software** that must exist on the OS. Emacs packages
(`elpa/`) install themselves from MELPA/ELPA on first launch and are not listed
here.

Every entry names the exact line in `init.el` that needs it, so you can drop
anything belonging to a language you don't use.

Status legend for this machine (checked 2026-07-28):
`[x]` present · `[ ]` missing · `[-]` intentionally not needed

---

## 0. TL;DR — clean Arch install

```bash
# Emacs + core tooling
sudo pacman -S --needed emacs git base-devel fd ripgrep pandoc-cli

# LSP servers + language toolchains (drop what you don't use)
sudo pacman -S --needed clang gopls go rust-analyzer rustup

# Rust components
rustup default stable
rustup component add rustfmt clippy

# Haskell (ghcup, not pacman — keeps GHC/HLS versions in sync)
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://get-ghcup.haskell.org | sh
ghcup install ghc   --set latest
ghcup install cabal --set latest
ghcup install hls   --set latest

# Fonts
sudo pacman -S --needed ttf-nerd-fonts-symbols
# Aporetic is AUR-only:
yay -S ttf-aporetic          # or: paru -S ttf-aporetic
```

Then, **inside Emacs**, run the post-install steps in §7 (icon fonts and
tree-sitter grammars — neither is a distro package).

---

## 1. Emacs itself

| | Package (Arch) | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `[x]` | `emacs` | Version **30.1+ required**. Config uses `setopt` (29+), built-in `use-package` (29+), built-in `which-key` (30+), and `treesit`. |

The **GUI build is required** — `emacs-nox` will not work correctly here:

| Build feature | Needed by | Verified on this machine |
|---|---|---|
| tree-sitter | the grammars in `tree-sitter/` | `(treesit-available-p)` → `t` |
| native compilation | `eln-cache/`; startup speed | `(native-comp-available-p)` → `t` |
| SVG rendering (librsvg) | `kind-icon` → `svg-lib` (corfu icons, `init.el:367`) | `svg` in `image-types` |
| native JSON | eglot throughput (`init.el:234`) | `json-parse-string` bound |
| dynamic modules | `treesit` grammar loading | `module-load` bound |

Arch's `extra/emacs` ships all five. If you build from source:
`--with-tree-sitter --with-native-compilation --with-rsvg --with-json`.

---

## 2. Core tooling (needed regardless of language)

| | Binary | Arch package | Needed by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `[x]` | `git` | `git` | projectile's primary indexer — `projectile-indexing-method 'alien` (`init.el:206`) runs `git ls-files -zco --exclude-standard` in every git project. Also `vc-follow-symlinks` (`init.el:43`) and tree-sitter grammar fetching (§7). |
| `[x]` | `find`, `grep` | `findutils`, `grep` | `consult-find` bound to `C-c C-f` (`init.el:219`) shells out to `find`; `consult-grep` uses `grep`. Both are in Arch `base` — listed for non-Arch distros. |
| `[x]` | `fd` | `fd` | Projectile prefers `fd` over `find` for **non-git** projects (`projectile-fd-executable`), and it is much faster. Also backs `consult-fd`. Strongly recommended, not strictly required. |
| `[x]` | `rg` | `ripgrep` | `consult-ripgrep`. Not bound to a key in your config, but reachable via `M-x` and worth having. Optional. |
| `[x]` | `pandoc` | `pandoc-cli` | `markdown-command` (`init.el:468`) is `pandoc --from=gfm --to=html5 --standalone`. Without it, `C-c C-c` in a Markdown buffer fails. Note the package is `pandoc-cli`, **not** `pandoc` (which is the Haskell library). |
| `[x]` | `gcc`, `make` | `base-devel` | Compiling tree-sitter grammars (§7) and native-comp's C toolchain. |

---

## 3. LSP servers

`eglot` auto-starts for these modes (`init.el:236-241`). A missing server means
eglot reports "no language server" and you get no completion/diagnostics for
that language, but nothing else breaks.

| | Binary | Arch package | Trigger |
|---|---|---|---|
| `[x]` | `clangd` | `clang` | `c-mode`, `c++-mode`, `c-ts-mode`, `c++-ts-mode` hooks. Configured with `--clang-tidy` and `-std=c23`. |
| `[x]` | `gopls` | `gopls` | `go-mode` hook (`init.el:241`). |
| `[x]` | `rust-analyzer` | `rust-analyzer` *or* `rustup component add rust-analyzer` | `rustic-mode` hook (`init.el:421`). Configured with `:check (:command "clippy")` — this requires `cargo-clippy`, see §4. |
| `[x]` | `haskell-language-server-wrapper` | **ghcup** (see §4) | `haskell-mode` hook. The `-wrapper` binary is what dispatches to the HLS build matching the project's GHC — do not install a bare `haskell-language-server`. |

> Note: the `clangd`/`rust-analyzer` extra arguments only take effect with the
> `eglot-server-programs` fix committed on the `develop` branch (`299a2d3`). On
> `master` the servers still run, just with eglot's stock arguments.

---

## 4. Language toolchains

Install only the languages you use.

### C / C++
| | Binary | Arch package | Needed by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `[x]` | `clang-format` | `clang` | `dk/clang-fos` (`src/functions.el:58`) adds a format-on-save hook — but **only in trees containing a `.clang-format` file**, so it is inert elsewhere. |
| `[x]` | `gcc` | `base-devel` | Compiling; also required by tree-sitter grammar builds. |

### Rust
| | Binary | Source | Needed by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `[x]` | `cargo` | `rustup` (or `rust`) | `rustic` drives all build/test/run through cargo. |
| `[x]` | `rustfmt` | `rustup component add rustfmt` | `rustic-format-on-save t` (`init.el:423`) — and `rust-format-on-save t` (`init.el:407`), which is redundant; see `claude.notes` §2. |
| `[x]` | `cargo-clippy` | `rustup component add clippy` | The `:check (:command "clippy")` option passed to rust-analyzer. Without it rust-analyzer falls back to `cargo check`. |

`rustup` and the distro `rust` package conflict — pick one. `rustup` is
recommended so `rustfmt`/`clippy`/`rust-analyzer` versions stay matched.

### Go
| | Binary | Arch package | Needed by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `[x]` | `go`, `gofmt` | `go` | `gofmt` is called by the `before-save-hook` at `init.el:413-415`. `gofmt` ships inside the `go` package — no separate install. |

### Haskell
| | Binary | Source | Needed by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `[x]` | `ghc` | ghcup | Compiler; HLS needs a matching version. |
| `[x]` | `cabal` | ghcup | `haskell-process-type 'cabal-repl` (`init.el:396`) — the `C-c C-z` REPL and `C-c C-l` load both go through `cabal repl`. |
| `[x]` | `haskell-language-server-wrapper` | ghcup | eglot (§3). |

Use **ghcup**, not pacman: HLS must be built against the exact GHC version, and
ghcup manages that pairing. Arch's `ghc` frequently drifts ahead of what HLS
supports. Remember to add `~/.ghcup/bin` and `~/.cabal/bin` to `PATH`.

---

## 5. Fonts

| | Font | Arch package | Needed by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `[x]` | **Aporetic Sans Mono** | `ttf-aporetic` — **AUR only**, use `yay`/`paru` | Hard-coded as the default and minibuffer face (`init.el:87-88`). Missing → silent fallback to a random monospace font, with no warning. |
| `[x]` | **Symbols Nerd Font** | `ttf-nerd-fonts-symbols` | `doom-modeline` (`init.el:96`) depends on `nerd-icons`, which renders tofu boxes without a Nerd Font — even though the rest of your config uses `all-the-icons`. |
| `[x]` | all-the-icons set | *not a distro package* | `all-the-icons` (`init.el:92`) and `all-the-icons-dired` (`init.el:195`). Installed from **inside Emacs** — see §7. |

Because `install.notes` mentions both families: `nerd-icons`, `nerd-icons-dired`
and `nerd-icons-corfu` are already in `elpa/` but unused by the config. If you
consolidate on nerd-icons (recommended — it works in the terminal, and
doom-modeline expects it), you can skip the all-the-icons font step entirely.

---

## 6. Tree-sitter grammars

`tree-sitter/` is in `.gitignore`, so **a fresh clone has no grammars**. They are
compiled locally, not installed by pacman. Requires `git` and `gcc`.

Currently present on this machine (9):
`bash` `c` `cmake` `cpp` `json` `python` `rust` `toml` `yaml`

> Caveat carried over from `claude.notes` §4.2: the config does not yet set
> `major-mode-remap-alist`, so **none of the `*-ts-mode` variants actually
> activate** and these grammars are currently unused. Install them anyway if you
> plan to apply that fix; otherwise this whole section is deferrable.

---

## 7. Post-install steps inside Emacs

These cannot be done by the package manager.

1. **First launch downloads ~60 ELPA packages.** Needs network + working TLS.
   Expect a slow first start; subsequent starts are fast.

2. **Icon fonts** (only if staying with all-the-icons):
   ```
   M-x all-the-icons-install-fonts
   ```

3. **Tree-sitter grammars** — per language:
   ```
   M-x treesit-install-language-grammar
   ```
   Or scripted, after adding the recipes to `treesit-language-source-alist`:
   ```elisp
   (dolist (lang '(bash c cpp cmake json python rust toml yaml))
     (unless (treesit-language-available-p lang)
       (treesit-install-language-grammar lang)))
   ```

4. **Create `~/org`** — `org-agenda-files` is `(list "~/org")` (`init.el:487`).
   If the directory does not exist, `org-agenda` errors out:
   ```bash
   mkdir -p ~/org
   ```

---

## 8. What you do *not* need

Listed to prevent over-installing:

| | Tool | Why not |
|---|---|---|
| `[-]` | `stack` | `haskell-process-type` is `'cabal-repl` (`init.el:396`), not stack. |
| `[-]` | `goimports` | Config uses `gofmt-before-save`, not goimports (`init.el:413`). |
| `[-]` | `multimarkdown` | Only referenced in the **commented-out** markdown block (`init.el:448`). The live config uses pandoc. |
| `[-]` | `tree-sitter` CLI | `treesit` loads the compiled `.so` directly; the Rust CLI is only for grammar *authors*. |
| `[-]` | `trash-cli` | `delete-by-moving-to-trash` (`init.el:44`) uses Emacs' own freedesktop trash implementation. |
| `[-]` | `libvterm` / `vterm` | No terminal package in this config. |
| `[-]` | `git-delta`, `difftastic` | No magit — see `claude.notes` §4.1. If you add magit, `git` alone is enough. |
| `[-]` | `sqlite`, `graphviz`, `LaTeX` | No org-roam, no org-babel graph/LaTeX export configured. |
| `[-]` | `aspell` / `hunspell` | No spellchecker configured. Worth adding for the Org/Markdown prose modes, but nothing currently calls one. |

---

## 9. Verification

Run after installing to see what the config will actually find:

```bash
for c in git gcc make find grep fd rg pandoc \
         clangd clang-format gopls go gofmt \
         rust-analyzer cargo rustfmt cargo-clippy \
         ghc cabal haskell-language-server-wrapper; do
  printf '%-34s %s\n' "$c" "$(command -v "$c" 2>/dev/null || echo 'MISSING')"
done

fc-list : family | grep -ciE 'aporetic'          # expect >= 1
fc-list : family | grep -ciE 'symbols nerd font' # expect >= 1
```

From inside Emacs, the authoritative check (it uses Emacs' own `exec-path`,
which can differ from your shell `PATH` when Emacs is started from a desktop
launcher rather than a terminal):

```elisp
(dolist (b '("clangd" "gopls" "rust-analyzer" "haskell-language-server-wrapper"
             "clang-format" "gofmt" "cabal" "pandoc" "fd" "git"))
  (message "%-34s %s" b (or (executable-find b) "MISSING")))
```

If the shell finds a binary but Emacs does not, that is the classic
launcher-PATH problem — see `claude.notes` §4.7 (`exec-path-from-shell`).

